  "conclusion": "The preserved-slice obstruction survives the full normalized family and any linear symplectic pre/post factors. Nontrivial folds do not beat radius 1 even before mixing, random post-mixing audits obey the sharper bound R >= delta^(-1/2), and random pre/post audits show that pre-mixing also fails to evade the same bound. This family does not repair the proposed solution.",
